    {
      "id": "claim_da08bbb7e77b4034b98591d63809591e",
      "statement": "utils/cautils defines a CaClient interface covering CA operations (Sign, Renew, RenewWithToken, Revoke, Rekey, SSH variants, Version, GetRootCAs, GetCaURL) that both the online smallstep/certificates ca client and the embedded OfflineCA satisfy, so ca commands share one code path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L29-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a000d1d60c28618e22b0902c70b819e3b30b8ab48eaededb488012c2aad4d575:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff7b6d5f7bbc4e37a8aa2d64d4c39f5a",
      "statement": "cautils.NewClient selects the offline path when the --offline flag is set (requiring --ca-config) and otherwise builds an online client from the parsed ca-url with --root defaulting to the STEPPATH root CA file pki.GetRootCAPath(), erroring with a required-flag error when that file is missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L52-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:728e02c9fda0397f940ca7b0af3633c0e94b12b6a90ea0c7f7b0dbc4d00b5619:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e9e1b6c8c50c4be4a212f7a3a6a1f89a",
      "statement": "flags.ParseCaURL enforces HTTPS-only CA URLs by assuming https when no scheme is present, rejecting other schemes, and repairing bare IPv6 hosts into bracketed form so host:port parsing succeeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://flags/flags.go#L645-L706",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5062a053429344ae599e9dce8b5f2197c74f76683ef0e7a310796cb3f44efc6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0757a0659295491bab2facc36b019a38",
      "statement": "OfflineCA is a package-level singleton wrapping an in-process smallstep/certificates authority.Authority built from the ca.json config; the cached instance avoids double initialization that can fail on storage locks such as BadgerDB, the config must contain at least one provisioner, and --password-file supplies the authority config password.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L36-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:535a7ad7ebf3f401a29b0c771c81fe1d6113871042646acb5be94508de7544d1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_de3e70d71d8c4bc8bf3635d077956754",
      "statement": "OfflineCA derives its CA URL and per-token-type audiences (/sign, /renew, /revoke, /ssh/sign, etc.) from the first DNSNames entry of ca.json, bracketing bare IPv6 addresses via toHostname.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L141-L163",
